-p, --password  <p>Specifies the password for authentication. This option is used in conjunction with <code>--auth basic</code> for HTTP Basic Authentication.</p>  <p>Note: Be cautious when using passwords in command-line arguments, as they may be visible in command history or process listings.</p>  <p>Usage: <pre><code>kodjin-cli --auth basic --password &lt;password&gt;
</code></pre></p> <p>Example:</p> <pre><code>$ kodjin-cli --auth basic --user admin --password secretpass install hl7.fhir.us.core@4.0.0
</code></pre>

-b, --bearer  <p>Specifies the bearer token for authentication. This option is used in conjunction with <code>--auth bearer</code> for Bearer Token Authentication.</p> <p>Usage: <pre><code>kodjin-cli --auth bearer --bearer &lt;token&gt;
</code></pre></p> <p>Example:</p> <pre><code>$ kodjin-cli --auth bearer --bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9... install hl7.fhir.us.core@4.0.0
</code></pre>

--request-timeout  <p>Limit the waiting time of the response to REQUEST_TIMEOUT (in seconds). The default value is 30 sec. If you want to wait more or less you can change this value by adding <code>--request-timeout</code> to the request.</p> <p>Usage: <pre><code>kodjin-cli --request-timeout &lt;number&gt;
</code></pre></p> <p>Example:</p> <p>In this example, we will increase waiting time for the response: <pre><code>$ kodjin-cli --request-timeout 40 install hl7.fhir.us.core@4.0.0
</code></pre></p>
